      "writtenOn": "2019-09-12T19:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From Rev 3.0, Section 6.2.1.1.7\n\n\" The 1-bit Cable Plug field Shalli ndicate whether this Message originated from a Cable Plug or VPD:\n• 0b Message originated from a DFP or UFP\nUSB Power Delivery Specification Revision 3.0, Version 2.0 Page 103\n• 1b Message originated from a Cable Plug or VPD\n\"\n\nThis check is performed inside pd_set_cable_rev(). That said, it doesn\u0027t disambiguate between Cable Plug and VPD (both are treated the same). \n\nDo we need to worry about VPD? The spec says it is a captive cable device, and doesn\u0027t support Alternate modes (so userspace likely won\u0027t do anything with this information anyway?)",
      "parentUuid": "44736830_3b838abf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1587,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1587,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "e52b89a5db1d365283fe477f34d17fdb4a1f5ea3",
